# opcode	semantic class; no unsupported opcode silently completes
# This table is interpreter dispatch, not a full-domain numerical certificate.
# The bounded replay gate is QSA convert/attend and sym NT4 gate_up/down.
# A row means the interpreter has a model for the name; the model itself refuses every unmeasured modifier or
# architecture at execution. Rows with an architecture-limited model: v_wmma_f32_16x16x16_bf16 (gfx1201 measured;
# gfx1151 historical corpus only, fresh receipt pending), v_dot2_f32_f16/bf16 (gfx1201 only), and the gfx1201-only
# SWMMAC rows v_swmmac_f32_16x16x32_f16/bf16 and v_swmmac_i32_16x16x32_iu8/iu4/x64_iu4 (index_key 0/1, measured
# neg_lo/neg_hi, integer two-half CLAMP; accumulator NEG[2], float CLAMP and other OPSEL bits refused).
# NO row, so a decoded program hard-errors at load: v_wmma_bf16_16x16x16_bf16, the 16-bit-out SWMMAC
# (f16/bf16 out) and every FP8/BF8 WMMA and SWMMAC.
# See isa/emu/float_edges.md "Opcode-fill qualification (pending)".
# v_log_f32_e32, v_rsq_f32_e32 and v_sqrt_f32_e32 are outside that gate;
# their candidate numeric paths remain unqualified for the full input domain.
